{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolumeConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolumeConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_two","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L276-L281","doc":"**Edge 2** reduces to the saddle cubic: `y²·(z′)³ = 1` iff `y² = (1−y)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_one","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L267-L274","doc":"**Edge 1** holds identically — it is `(z·z′·z″)² = (−1)² = 1`, and needs no\ncubic at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.edge_zero","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L259-L265","doc":"**Edge 0** reduces to the saddle cubic: `y²·z′·(z″)⁴ = 1` iff `y² = (1−y)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_sq_eq_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_sq_eq_cube","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L255-L257","doc":"The branch form of the cubic: `y² = (1−y)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.one_sub_fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.one_sub_fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L252-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L249-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoGluing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoGluing","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L243-L247","doc":"SnapPy's three 5₂ edge-gluing equations, as exponent data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_volume_dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_volume_dilog","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L215-L220","doc":"And in dilogarithm form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_volume","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L199-L213","doc":"**`volume (5₂ triangulation) = VOL_5_2`.**\n\nNot by assuming the shapes are equal — they are not — but because the volume is\ninvariant under the relabelling that relates them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_middle_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_middle_shape","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L195-L197","doc":"The middle tetrahedron's shape is `1/(1 − y₁)`, matching SnapPy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_two","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L192-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_one","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L189-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation_tet_zero","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L186-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTriangulation","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L164-L184","doc":"**The 5₂ ideal triangulation**, with SnapPy's actual shapes.\n\n⚠ **CORRECTION (2026-08-09).**  An earlier version of this file defined the\ntriangulation as `const 3 fiveTwoTet` — three tetrahedra all of shape `y₁`.\n**That is wrong**, and SnapPy says so: `Manifold('5_2').tetrahedra_shapes` gives\n\n    tet 0 : 0.78492014550 + 1.30714127868i   = y₁\n    tet 1 : 0.12256116688 + 0.74486176662i   = 1/(1 − y₁)   ← NOT y₁\n    tet 2 : 0.78492014550 + 1.30714127868i   = y₁\n\nThe middle tetrahedron carries the *second edge parameter* of `y₁`, not `y₁`.\n\nThe volume claim survives — but as a **theorem now, not an assumption**: the\nrelabelling `z ↦ 1/(1−z)` cyclically permutes the three dihedral angles\n(`IdealTetrahedron.rotate_angles`), so `Λ(θ₁)+Λ(θ₂)+Λ(θ₃)` is unchanged\n(`volume_rotate`).  That is why `Vol = 3·D(y₁)` despite the shapes differing.\n\nRecorded because the earlier version was a guess that happened to give the right\nnumber for a reason it did not state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoTet","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L160-L162","doc":"The 5₂ ideal tetrahedron: shape `y₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_law_of_sines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_law_of_sines","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L142-L146","doc":"The ideal-tetrahedron law of sines at the 5₂ shape:\n`‖y₁‖ = sin θ₂ / sin θ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_angles_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_angles_sum","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L136-L140","doc":"The three dihedral angles of the 5₂ tetrahedron sum to `π` — a consistency\ncheck that `fiveTwoShape` is a genuine ideal-tetrahedron shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2_two_forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2_two_forms","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L128-L134","doc":"Both forms at once, as the pair a reader most likely wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2_eq_dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2_eq_dilog","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L116-L126","doc":"**The dilogarithm form of `VOL_5_2`.**\n\nImmediate from `KummerRadial.kummer` at `y₁`.  Before Kummer this equation could\nnot have been written down: `BlochWigner_lob` is built from `arg`s and\n`BlochWignerLobachevsky.lean` explicitly forbade transporting dilogarithm facts\nonto it.  That prohibition is now lifted on `{Im z > 0}`, and `y₁` is there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.VOL_5_2","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**`VOL_5_2`, exactly** — three ideal tetrahedra of shape `y₁`, in the\nLobachevsky (angle) form.\n\nDefined, not derived: this is the exact transcendental target that `VOL_4_1`'s\n`qou-yf47` repair established as the corpus's convention.  The identification\nwith the hyperbolic volume of `S³ ∖ 5₂` is cited, not proved — see the module\nheader. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L101-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.fiveTwoShape","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L95-L97","doc":"**The 5₂ shape parameter** `y₁`: the root of `X³ − 2X² + 3X − 1` with\npositive imaginary part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.saddle","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The 5₂ root data, built from that real root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.realRoot_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.realRoot_spec","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L87-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolume.realRoot","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoVolumeConstant.lean#L83-L85","doc":"The real root of the saddle cubic in `(0,1)`, from the intermediate value\ntheorem. ","signatureChunk":0}]}